How can I create a GPT model that is capable of handling multi-modal inputs, including audio and image, while being time-sensitive in processing?
Here is a specific example of Go code that integrates audio and image inputs into the GPT model:
```go
// Load image and audio data
imgData, err := ioutil.ReadFile("image.jpg")
if err != nil {
    log.Fatal(err)
}
audioData, err := ioutil.ReadFile("audio.wav")
if err != nil {
    log.Fatal(err)
}
// Convert image and audio data to tensors
imgTensor, err := tf.NewTensor(string(imgData))
if err != nil {
    log.Fatal(err)
}
audioTensor, err := tf.NewTensor(string(audioData))
if err != nil {
    log.Fatal(err)
}
// Load pre-trained GPT model
model, err := tf.LoadSavedModel("path/to/saved/model", []string{"serve"}, nil)
if err != nil {
    log.Fatal(err)
}
// Run inference on multi-modal inputs
start := time.Now()
result, err := model.Session.Run(
    map[tf.Output]*tf.Tensor{
        model.Graph.Operation("serving_default_image_input").Output(0): imgTensor,
        model.Graph.Operation("serving_default_audio_input").Output(0): audioTensor,
    },
    []tf.Output{
        model.Graph.Operation("StatefulPartitionedCall").Output(0),
    },
    nil,
)
if err != nil {
    log.Fatal(err)
}
elapsed := time.Since(start)
// Process output
output := result[0].Value().(string)
fmt.Println("Output:", output)
fmt.Println("Inference time:", elapsed)
```
This code loads image and audio data, converts them to tensors, and feeds them into a pre-trained GPT model. The model then outputs a response based on the multi-modal inputs, and the code prints the output and the time it took to process the inputs. With this implementation, the GPT model is capable of accurately and efficiently processing multi-modal inputs in a time-sensitive manner.

How can I generate a passphrase in Swift that follows the guidelines of including at least 12 words and three words from a non-Indo-European language family?
