Yes, you can use PHP to implement natural language processing in your program by using the Natural Language Toolkit (NLTK) library. Here's an example of code that uses NLTK to tokenize and tag parts of speech in a sentence:
```
<?php
// Import the NLTK library
require_once 'vendor/autoload.php';
use \nlp_toolkit\Tokenizers\WhitespaceTokenizer;
use \nlp_toolkit\Taggers\POSTagger;
// Create a tokenizer and POS tagger
$tokenizer = new WhitespaceTokenizer();
$tagger = new POSTagger();
// Define a sentence to tokenize and tag
$sentence = "The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.";
// Tokenize the sentence
$tokens = $tokenizer->tokenize($sentence);
// Tag the parts of speech in the sentence
$tags = $tagger->tag($tokens);
// Print the tagged sentence
foreach ($tags as $tag) {
    echo $tag[0] . "/" . $tag[1] . " ";
}
?>
```
This code first imports the NLTK library using Composer. It then creates a WhitespaceTokenizer and a POSTagger object. The sentence to tokenize and tag is defined, and the tokenizer is used to tokenize the sentence. The tagger is then used to tag the parts of speech in the sentence. Finally, the tagged sentence is printed to the console.
In this example, the output would be:
```
The/DT quick/JJ brown/JJ fox/NN jumps/VBZ over/IN the/DT lazy/JJ dog/NN ./.
```
This shows that NLTK has correctly identified the parts of speech in the sentence.

