```
In this example, we have a base class called Animal with properties for name, age, and carnivore. We then have three subclasses: Mammal, Cat, and Dog, that inherit from the Animal class. The Mammal class has an additional property for breed, the Cat class has a property for fur color, and the Dog class has a property for breed and an additional method for performing tricks.
We can then deserialize the XML data into instances of these classes using the following code:
```
string xml = @"<Animals>
                  <Animal>
                    <Name>Lion</Name>
                    <Age>10</Age>
                    <Carnivore>true</Carnivore>
                  </Animal>
                  <Mammal>
                    <Name>Dog</Name>
