What are some steps I can take in my Java program to limit the amount of time my child can spend playing video games?
One approach could be to implement a timer that limits the amount of time the game can be played in one session. Here's an example Java code:
import java.util.Timer;
import java.util.TimerTask;
public class GameTimer {
  private Timer timer;
  private int secondsLeft;
  public GameTimer(int seconds) {
    secondsLeft = seconds;
    timer = new Timer();
    timer.schedule(new GameTimerTask(), 0, 1000);
  }
  public void cancel() {
    timer.cancel();
  }
  private class GameTimerTask extends TimerTask {
    public void run() {
      if (secondsLeft <= 0) {
        cancel();
        System.out.println("Game session over.");
        // add code to stop the game here
      } else {
        System.out.println("Time remaining: " + secondsLeft + " seconds");
        secondsLeft--;
      }
    }
  }
}
You can use this timer in your game code to limit the amount of time your child can spend playing. Simply create a GameTimer object with the desired time limit in seconds, and start it when the game session begins. The timer will run in the background and automatically stop the game session when the time limit is reached.

